Orry wrote:
>
> Dungeon level 3, for some reason I decided to attack a floating eye.
>
> It froze me and a group of were-jackals came and killed me while I
> couldn't move.

It's a lesson learned by all players.  There are monsters that actively
kill you, and there are monsters that have indirect dangers.  The
floating eye is one of the ones that have indirect dangers.

Once I learned missile combat ("Q" to put daggers in the quiver then "f"
to fire them or got plain "t" to throw items) floating eyes should have
stopped being a problem.  I play with color turned on so their blue "e"
tends to fade into the background - I still occasionally lose characters
to making a typo near floating eyes.  It happens less and less over time
but it's never quite stopped for me.

You're doing fine for a new player.  Try to learn a lesson from each
death.  Are you descending so fast you get in a crowd and die?  Are you
descending so slow you starve?  Are you running away from danger soon
enough so you can heal?  Are you learning the abilities of the various
items as you play game after game?  Nethack is a gigantic puzzle.


